<div class="price-intent-note"><strong>Important:</strong> Ram Mandir entry and any special access follow the temple administration's current rules. Please do not treat a private tour quotation as a guaranteed VIP queue bypass or a confirmed Mangla Aarti ticket. We discuss only the assistance and arrangements actually available for your date.</div>
<h2>How we would plan a one-day Ayodhya visit</h2>
<p>With just one day, begin with the temple that matters most to you. We generally protect a substantial block of time for <strong>Shri Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir</strong> because security, approach routes and crowds can change without much warning. Hanuman Garhi and Kanak Bhawan can be fitted around that visit, with the Ram Ki Paidi or Saryu riverfront added if time and energy permit.</p>
<p>It is tempting to add every temple seen on a map, but old Ayodhya works differently from an ordinary city tour. Private vehicles cannot reach every entrance. You may need an e-rickshaw followed by walking, and the final approach can be around 700–1,500 metres depending on restrictions. Tell us in advance if anyone is elderly or has difficulty walking.</p>
