<h2>Two days in Ayodhya: our preferred first-visit plan</h2>
<p>Two days are more comfortable for a family pilgrimage. On the first afternoon, explore <strong>Ram Ki Paidi</strong>, Kale Ram Mandir and Nageshwarnath, then enjoy time by the Saryu. If river conditions and current regulations permit, an afternoon boat ride can be requested separately. We would plan this before sunset rather than assume evening boating will operate.</p>
<p>On the second day, make an early start for Ram Mandir darshan, followed by Hanuman Garhi and Kanak Bhawan. This order is adjusted to the confirmed access rules and the group's needs. A guide can make the visit easier to understand, but temple security and queue conditions remain outside any operator's control.</p>
<p>For the detailed programme, see our <a href="/tours/ayodhya-tour-in-two-days/">private two-day Ayodhya tour</a>. A Saryu Aarti arrangement, front seating or Deep Daan can be discussed and added only after the local arrangements are checked for your dates.</p>
<h2>Is a three-day Ayodhya tour worth the additional cost?</h2>
<p>For senior travellers, families with children or guests who want time for prayer rather than constant sightseeing, the third day is valuable. It creates space to revisit a favourite temple or enjoy the riverfront more slowly. Optional visits towards <strong>Guptar Ghat, Nandigram or Chhapaiya</strong> can be considered after checking travel time and the final service scope.</p>
<p>Those outlying excursions are not automatically included simply because you book three days. We will identify any additional driving, guide services or entrance arrangements before confirming the price. See the <a href="/tours/ayodhya-tour-in-three-days/">three-day tour programme</a> for the core option.</p>
<h2>How much does Ayodhya cost from Lucknow or Varanasi?</h2>
<p>These published Ayodhya rates assume the local programme described on the tour pages. Starting in <strong>Lucknow</strong> or <strong>Varanasi</strong> adds an intercity journey and may change the vehicle duty, tolls and number of practical sightseeing hours. A same-day Lucknow–Ayodhya–Lucknow private tour is possible for some groups, but its quotation is not the same as the Ayodhya local one-day starting price.</p>
<p>Send us your flight or train timings, hotel location, passenger count and luggage details. We can quote the correct route instead of giving you a misleading per-person amount. Travellers combining both sacred cities can also consider our <a href="/tours/5-days-varanasi-ayodhya-tour-1/">Varanasi and Ayodhya private journey</a>.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions about Ayodhya tour pricing</h2>
<h3>Are hotels included in the Ayodhya packages?</h3><p>No. The published rates above are for the described ground services without accommodation. We can recommend hotels near the temple and quote rooms separately according to date and category.</p>
<h3>Can a solo traveller book a private Ayodhya tour?</h3><p>Yes. However, one guest does not pay the two-guest per-person starting rate because the private vehicle and guide costs are shared by fewer people. Ask us for a solo quotation.</p>
<h3>Does the package guarantee Ram Mandir VIP darshan?</h3><p>No. All entry and special-access arrangements depend on the temple administration's procedures and availability. We will clearly identify what, if anything, can be assisted or prearranged.</p>
<h3>Do senior citizens need to walk to Ram Mandir?</h3><p>Usually there is still a last-mile approach despite private transport. Let us know about mobility restrictions or wheelchair needs before booking. See our <a href="/travel-guide/ayodhya-ram-mandir-wheelchair-assistance/">Ayodhya wheelchair assistance guide</a> for practical considerations.</p>
<h3>Are the rates fixed during festivals?</h3><p>No. These are indicative regular-date starting prices reviewed in November 2026. Festival surcharges, local movement restrictions and special arrangements require reconfirmation.</p>
<p><strong>Ready to visit?</strong> Share the dates, number of adults and children, your arrival city, and whether your priority is Ram Mandir darshan, the Saryu or a more comprehensive pilgrimage. We will suggest a private programme and confirm the total before you decide.</p>
